						"value": "SLIT SCANNER\n\nThe Slit Scanner effect is based on Slit-scan photography.\nThis is a technique in which objects are placed on a image scanner and moved around while the scanner is active, creating distorted and warped images.\nBesides photography the technique is also used in film (Doctor Who, Vertigo, 2001: A Space Odyssey).\n\nIn this patch we are recreating a version of the Slit Scanner.\nThere are many ways you could adopt this technique and we strongly encourage you to take this patch and modify it. Especially because this digital format allows for slit scanners that would be be near impossible to build in a physical form.\n\nMaybe add some horizontal scanning?  Modulate the slit size with Perlin Noise? Luma Key the texture before scanning? Rotate the slit? Scan each color channel at a different rate? Go wild!"
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 293.0247802734375,
					"width": 574.51776123046875,
					"x": -1993.388427734375,
					"y": -958.1990966796875
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffd0c117",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"85": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "POSITION THE SLIT\n\nA slit has two properties: a position and a size.\nImagine putting your hand under an image scanner and moving it, that is the position and the resolution of the scanner is the size.\n\nHere we are taking the Texture and using Transform to move it around.\nBy using the widht of the patch, from the Patch Info node, we make sure the patch will run at any resolution.\nNote that we are sending the Slit Position parameter down to a Hub and into the next section of the patch: the scanner size."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 616.88751220703125,
					"width": 1528.6871337890625,
					"x": -2000.341064453125,
					"y": -626.6422119140625
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffae7bff",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"86": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "SLIT SIZE\n\nChanging the size of the slit is done with a Crop node.\nSince we are moving the texture to the left with the Slit Position slider, we are cropping it from the right side.\nBy using the Slit Position and Slit Size slider the user can pick wich part of the texture they would like to slit scan and how big that slit should be."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 616.88751220703125,
					"width": 1528.6871337890625,
					"x": -1658.2034912109375,
					"y": 48.025726318359375
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffe53357",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"87": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "SCANNING\n\nThe scanning is done by creating a feedback loop with a Video Mixer.\nEach frame in the loop gets moved slightly to the right by the Transform node.\nThe amount of movement to the right is controlled by the Scan Speed slider."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 487.108795166015625,
					"width": 954.63751220703125,
					"x": 339.039947509765625,
					"y": 274.64898681640625
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffff6a00",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"88": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "SHOW SLIT & OUTPUT\n\nWe are taking the slit and putting it into a Switch with a Boolean In to control wheter the scanning or slit is displayed.\nThis allows the user to see how the slit looks.\nThis is a little debugging tool for the user, as with feedback it can get hard to track what is actually happening."
					}
				},
